      },
      "claims": {
        "summary": "GA acute hospital added about $0.7M, led by Cellulitis without MCC at about $0.3M and Kidney and Urinary Tract Infections without MCC at about $0.2M, with 68 more admissions across those two drivers. GA clinical concentration added about $1.0M, led by UTI SITE NOT SPECIFIED at about $0.4M and lower-limb cellulitis diagnoses at about $0.3M combined. GA physical rehab added about $0.3M across aftercare episodes, including 9 more admissions and higher paid per admit in the largest rehab cells."
      }
